---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import PageHero from '../components/PageHero.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="Privacy Notice"
  description="How Shemar Marks handles project inquiries, reference submissions, permissions, and privacy-respectful website measurement."
>
  <PageHero
    label="PRIVACY / UPDATED 19 OCTOBER 2026"
    title="Your details."
    accent="Handled with care."
    description="This notice explains how information submitted through this website is used. For questions or requests, contact hello@shemarmarks.com."
  />
  <section class="section wrap prose">
    <h2>Who handles your information.</h2>
    <p>
      Shemar Marks is an independent consultant based in Jamaica. Contact{' '}
      <a href="mailto:hello@shemarmarks.com">hello@shemarmarks.com</a> about access, correction,
      deletion, or withdrawing a reference.
    </p>
    <h2>Inquiries.</h2>
    <p>
      The inquiry form collects your name, email, project details, selected service, timeline, and
      any optional company, website, or budget information you provide. It also records the
      submitting page, CTA, landing page, referrer, campaign parameters, and submission time. This
      information is used to respond, scope work, and understand which pages generate useful
      inquiries.
    </p>
    <p>
      Submissions are stored at the edge before an attempt to synchronize them to a private CRM or
      send an acknowledgment. Cloudflare provides hosting, spam protection, and storage. Resend may
      deliver acknowledgment emails when configured. These providers may process information outside
      your country.
    </p>
    <h2>References.</h2>
    <p>
      Reference submissions are private until reviewed and approved. Your email is never part of the
      public reference. Your name, title, and company are displayed only with identity permission. A
      project value requires permission or an authorized owner entry, plus separate publication
      approval. You can request correction or removal by email.
    </p>
    <h2>Security and retention.</h2>
    <p>
      Please do not submit passwords, tokens, or sensitive business records. Access to submissions
      is restricted. Spam-prevention counters use a short-lived salted hash of the network address
      rather than retaining the raw address in the application database. Unconverted inquiries and
      pending references should be reviewed for deletion within 12 months; active engagement records
      may need to be retained for operational or contractual reasons.
    </p>
    <h2>Website measurement.</h2>
    <p>
      Cloudflare Web Analytics can provide aggregate page measurement when enabled. First-party
      event counts record page views and interactions without persistent visitor identifiers. Form
      attribution uses session storage within the current tab. Do Not Track and Global Privacy
      Control disable first-party interaction measurement.
    </p>
    <div class="privacy-controls">
      <label class="checkbox">
        <input id="analytics-optout" type="checkbox" />
        Disable first-party interaction measurement on this device.
      </label>
      <p class="small">
        This stores a local preference. Essential spam protection and submitted inquiry metadata
        still apply.
      </p>
    </div>
    <h2>External links.</h2>
    <p>
      Links to GitHub, LinkedIn, X, and other third parties are governed by those services’ own
      notices. Clicking an email link opens your chosen email application.
    </p>
  </section>
  <script>
    const checkbox = document.querySelector<HTMLInputElement>('#analytics-optout');
    if (checkbox) {
      try {
        checkbox.checked = localStorage.getItem('sm-analytics') === 'off';
      } catch {}
      checkbox.addEventListener('change', () => {
        try {
          localStorage.setItem('sm-analytics', checkbox.checked ? 'off' : 'on');
        } catch {}
      });
    }
  </script>
</Layout>
